        <id>https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27505</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27505"/>
        <updated>2025-08-05T14:54:01.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/>
<h4 dir="auto">Summary</h4>
<p dir="auto">Chrome 139 adds support for the <code class="notranslate">corner-shape</code> property, and its related shorthands and longhand. The properties have already been added to BCD by the collector, but the types that it can take as values have not.</p>
<p dir="auto">This PR adds data for the types.</p>
<p dir="auto">Note that I have included two data points for <code class="notranslate">superellipse()</code> — one for the function itself, and one for the use of <code class="notranslate">superellipse()</code> as a <code class="notranslate">&lt;corner-shape-value&gt;</code>. I thought this was a good idea in case <code class="notranslate">superellipse()</code> has more parameter options added, or is used as a possible value for other properties in the future.</p>

<h4 dir="auto">Test results and supporting details</h4>


